  <layout>One block of verse in a single column, centred on the page; a printed page number at the top right corner; no running head; no margin notes; a small mark at the bottom left of the text.</layout>
  <page_number>180</page_number>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Ignava fugiens tædia inertiæ?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Non plures tumidis hostibus inclyta</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Victis Marte Duces exuvias ferunt.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4" para="true">
      <i>Hæc dulci satagit quæ placeant Ciro,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Iussisque obsequitur legitimis lubens.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Solers cuncta fugit noxia quæ putat,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Et quærit Vigili commoda pectore.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8" para="true">
      <i>Lanas Vsque domum, linaq; canuebit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Exercetque colos, filaque diuidens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Pannos docta manu texere conficit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Telarumque parat sedula copiam.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12" para="true">
      <i>Non quæ littus arat sapius exterum,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Et fluctus Volitat per maris hospiti</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Nauis plura refert commoda nauitæ</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Multo farre graui merceque barbara.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16" para="true">
      <i>Somnos illa oculis excutiens prius</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Surgit, purpureum quàm iubar exerat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Aurora, &amp; nitidis aurea sydērum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Collucere polo agmina definant.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20" para="true">
      <i>Promisumque suis temporibus penu</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Prudens distribuit: penfaque protinus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Partitur famulis iusta fidelibus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Iussumque Vrget opus, nec tolerat moras.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24" para="true">
      <i>Agros cauta notat queis sobolescere</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Frugum semper amat fertilior seges.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Venalesque sibi diuite comparat</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Two-line mark at the foot (a small stroke, possibly a catchword or stain) not transcribed. Some words are doubtful: "Ignava" may read "Ignava"; "Vsque" and "Vigili" and "Vrget" follow the printed capitals; "farre" as printed; "sydērum" as printed with a macron-like mark. Line "Non quæ littus arat sapius exterum" reads as printed in the scan.</notes>
</page>
